{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00352 - MONDO_18435",
  "verbalization": "Tioguanine is implicated in the treatment of Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through a series of interconnected indications. The evidence suggests that Tioguanine is linked to AML through the use of Glasdegib and Idarubicin, both of which are indicated for AML with specific genetic alterations. This pathway highlights a potential mechanism where Tioguanine may influence the treatment of AML by targeting pathways associated with topoisomerase inhibitors, which are known to interact with the Inv3(p21;q26.2) or T(3;3)(p21;q26.2) genetic abnormalities. The overlapping indications for Tioguanine and these specific AML subtypes suggest a possible role in the therapeutic management of AML with these genetic markers. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering the broader context of drug indications and their potential interactions in the treatment of AML.",
